# This repo dogfoods the layout it ships, so its own operating files live under
# .shell-team/. Ignoring `.shell-team/` globally is a reasonable thing for an
# adopter to do (see the README's note on deciding whether to track the base
# dir), and a global core.excludesFile that does so would hide these files here
# too. Re-include the directory explicitly: this repo tracks its own board,
# specs, retros, and curated reviews as versioned project records.
!.shell-team/

# Raw review dumps and telemetry are never committed.
# Mirrors the hygiene rule this project adopted after a 2026 PII incident:
# curated review notes are tracked, raw transcripts and run logs are not.
# `.shell-team/.gitignore` already covers `runs/` telemetry and the
# codex-capture temps; these patterns add the raw review dumps, which the
# shipped base-dir template deliberately leaves to the host repo.
.shell-team/reviews/*.txt
.shell-team/reviews/*.json
.shell-team/reviews/*.jsonl
.codex-review.json

# NOTE: `.shell-team/rollups` is deliberately NOT ignored — roll-up summaries
# are meant to be tracked (tests/rollup-track/run.sh asserts this).

# Personal, per-checkout configuration. How much the session checks in with you
# is a working preference, not a property of the project, so these stay out of
# git — see docs/tuning-oversight.md.
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
